DESCRIPTION:Assignment Overview\n\nYou are tasked with developing and desig
 ning a small application that incorporates the use of external APIs. This 
 assignment is divided into two main parts. In Part One\, you will implemen
 t the application locally\, and in Part Two\, you will deploy the applicat
 ion on the web servers you have been working on so far. The goal is to cre
 ate an application that serves a meaningful purpose\, providing genuine va
 lue to users\, rather than being a gimmick. For example\, applications lik
 e random joke generators\,cat facts generators\, weather application\, foo
 d menu apps\, and currency and timeZone converters would not meet this cri
 terion.\n\nPart One: Local Implementation\n\nIn the first part of the assi
 gnment\, you will develop an application that runs locally on your machine
 . You have the flexibility to choose between creating a Command-Line Inter
 face (CLI) application or a web application with a frontend built using HT
 ML\, CSS\, and JavaScript. The core focus here is to effectively utilize e
 xternal APIs to fetch and display relevant data within your application.\n
 \nIt's crucial to thoroughly read the documentation for each API you plan 
 to use. Pay attention to details such as endpoints\, methods of accessing 
 API keys\, rate limits\, and any other pertinent information. You are enco
 uraged to refer to reputable external APIs\, such as those available on [R
 apidAPI] (https://rapidapi.com/categories)\, or any other reliable sources
 . Be diligent in vetting any public APIs to ensure they are secure and fre
 e from malicious content.\n\nYour application should present the retrieved
  data in an easy-to-understand format\, allowing users to interact with it
  meaningfully—such as sorting\, filtering\, or searching through the dat
 a. The user interface should be intuitive\, enhancing the overall user exp
 erience whether it's through a CLI or a graphical interface.\n\nPart Two: 
 Deployment\n\nThe second part involves deploying your application to make 
 it accessible online. You are provided with access to three web servers: t
 wo standard web servers (Web01 and Web02) and one load balancer (Lb01). Yo
 ur task is to deploy your application on both standard web servers and con
 figure the load balancer to distribute incoming traffic between them.\n\nB
 y setting up the load balancer\, you ensure that your application can hand
 le requests efficiently\, providing reliability and scalability. Users acc
 essing your application via the load balancer's address should experience 
 seamless performance\, regardless of which server handles their request.\n
 \nIn your README file\, include detailed instructions on how you deployed 
 your application to the servers and how you configured the load balancer. 
 Explain the steps taken and any configurations made to ensure the load bal
 ancer correctly interacts with the web servers. Testing is essential here\
 ; verify that your application functions as intended when accessed through
  the load balancer and that traffic is appropriately balanced between the 
 two servers.\n\nApplication Requirements\n\nYour application must serve a 
 real and practical purpose\, addressing a genuine need or problem. While a
 pplications for entertainment are acceptable\, they should offer substanti
 al value beyond mere amusement. Utilize at least one external API\, ensuri
 ng you provide proper credit to the API developers in your documentation. 
 Handle API keys and any sensitive information securely\; do not expose the
 m in your public repository.\n\nEnable user interaction with the data pres
 ented in your application. This could involve features like sorting data s
 ets\, filtering results based on specific criteria\, or searching for part
 icular information. Present the data clearly and logically to facilitate e
 asy comprehension. Additionally\, implement error handling to manage poten
 tial issues gracefully\, such as API downtime or invalid responses.\n\nBon
 us Tasks (Optional for Extra Points)\n\nFor those interested in extending 
 their project and earning extra points\, there are optional tasks availabl
 e that will not affect your normal grade. These include:\n\n* Implementing
  enhanced features like user authentication\, personalized user settings\,
  or advanced data visualization tools to enrich user experience.\n\n* Opti
 mizing your application for performance\, such as by implementing caching 
 mechanisms for API responses to reduce load times and improve efficiency.\
 n\n* Enhancing scalability by utilizing containerization tools like Docker
 \, and orchestration tools like Kubernetes\, to manage your application's 
 deployment in a more robust environment.\n\n* Setting up a Continuous Inte
 gration/Continuous Deployment (CI/CD) pipeline to automate the testing and
  deployment processes\, thereby streamlining development workflows.\n\n* I
 mplementing advanced security measures\, including thorough input validati
 on and protection against common vulnerabilities like SQL injection and cr
 oss-site scripting (XSS) attacks.\n\nThese tasks are entirely optional and
  are intended to challenge you further while providing an opportunity to d
 elve deeper into advanced topics.\n\nDeliverables\n\nYou are required to s
 ubmit a link to your GitHub repository containing all of your source code.
  Make sure to include a .gitignore file to exclude unnecessary files and t
 o prevent sensitive information\, such as API keys\, from being uploaded. 
 You are to provide all the necessary API keys in the comment section. All 
 necessary credentials needed to access the application(Login details inclu
 sive).\n\nAlongside your code\, you need to provide a short demo video tha
 t is no longer than two minutes. This video should demonstrate how to use 
 your application locally and how to access it via the load balancer. Highl
 ight the key features and functionalities\, showcasing the user interactio
 n and the application's response to various inputs.\n\nYour README file sh
 ould be comprehensive\, containing clear instructions on how to run your a
 pplication locally and how to deploy it to the provided web servers. Inclu
 de information about the APIs you used\, with links to their official docu
 mentation. Share any challenges you encountered during development and how
  you overcame them. Don't forget to credit the API developers and any othe
 r resources or libraries you utilized in your project.\n\nRequirements\n\n
 All the code submitted must be your original work. Submissions will underg
 o plagiarism checks to ensure authenticity. The demo video should strictly
  not exceed two minutes in length.\n\nEnsure that your code is clean\, rea
 dable\, and well-documented. Adhere to best practices relevant to the prog
 ramming languages and frameworks you employ. Properly credit all external 
 APIs and third-party resources\, and handle all API keys and sensitive dat
 a securely.\n\nDeadline\n\nPlease be aware that there is a strict deadline
  for this assignment: Saturday\, March 29. No extensions will be granted b
 eyond this date unless you have a Mitigating Circumstance\, so manage your
  time accordingly to ensure you meet all the requirements by the deadline.
 \n\nGrading Criteria\n\nYour work will be evaluated based on the following
  criteria:\n\n* Functionality (50%): How effectively your application meet
 s the outlined functional requirements\, including the efficient use of ex
 ternal APIs and the provision of a meaningful\, valuable service to users.
 \n\n* Deployment (20%): The successful deployment of your application on t
 he provided web servers and the proper configuration and utilization of th
 e load balancer to manage traffic.\n\n* User Experience (10%): The degree 
 to which your application is user-friendly and intuitive\, with clear pres
 entation of data and ease of navigation.\n\n* Documentation (10%): The qua
 lity and thoroughness of your README file\, including clear instructions\,
  proper credits\, and comprehensive explanations.\n\n* Demo Video (10%): H
 ow effectively your demo video showcases the application's features within
  the allotted time\, demonstrating both functionality and user interaction
 .\n\nSubmission Instructions\n\nTo submit your assignment\, provide the UR
 L to your GitHub repository containing your source code. Also\, in the git
 hub readme file include the link to your demo video\, which can be hosted 
 on a platform of your choice such as YouTube or Vimeo\, a link to the depl
 oyed website. Ensure that all links and resources you provide are accessib
 le and not restricted\, allowing for a smooth review process. Missing link
 s will lead to significant loss of marks and a zero if the github reposito
 ry is private or missing.\n\n \n\nNote: Any assignment without a demo vid
 eo or API KEYS or Necessary credentials will be given a zero.\n\nGood Luck
 !\n\n 
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Playing Around with APIs [Web_Infrastructure]
