 ou meet all the requirements by the deadline.</p>\n<p><strong>Grading Crit
 eria</strong></p>\n<p>Your work will be evaluated based on the following c
 riteria:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Functionality (50%)</strong>: How effectiv
 ely your application meets the outlined functional requirements\, includin
 g the efficient use of external APIs and the provision of a meaningful\, v
 aluable service to users.</li>\n<li><strong>Deployment (20%)</strong>: The
  successful deployment of your application on the provided web servers and
  the proper configuration and utilization of the load balancer to manage t
 raffic.</li>\n<li><strong>User Experience (10%)</strong>: The degree to wh
 ich your application is user-friendly and intuitive\, with clear presentat
 ion of data and ease of navigation.</li>\n<li><strong>Documentation (10%)<
 /strong>: The quality and thoroughness of your README file\, including cle
 ar instructions\, proper credits\, and comprehensive explanations.</li>\n<
 li><strong>Demo Video (10%)</strong>: How effectively your demo video show
 cases the application's features within the allotted time\, demonstrating 
 both functionality and user interaction.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Submissio
 n Instructions</strong></p>\n<p>To submit your assignment\, provide the UR
 L to your GitHub repository containing your source code. Also\, in the git
 hub readme file include the link to your demo video\, which can be hosted 
 on a platform of your choice such as YouTube or Vimeo\, a link to the depl
 oyed website. Ensure that all links and resources you provide are accessib
 le and not restricted\, allowing for a smooth review process. Missing link
 s will lead to significant loss of marks and a zero if the github reposito
 ry is private or missing.</p>\n<p>&nbsp\;</p>\n<p>Note: Any assignment wit
 hout a demo video or API KEYS or Necessary credentials will be given a zer
 o.</p>\n<p><strong>Good Luck!</strong></p>\n<p>&nbsp\;</p>
